card.statement:
Let $\varepsilon\in\mathbb R$,
$0<\varepsilon <1/3$, and let a
sequence of positive real numbers

\begin{equation*}
\delta_1,\
\mu_1,\
\delta_2,\
\mu_2,\
\delta_3,\
\mu_3,\ \dots
\end{equation*}

be defined by induction:

\begin{equation*}
\delta_1=\mu_1:=\varepsilon^5,\qquad
\delta_{i+1}
:=\varepsilon^{-1}\delta_i\mu _i,\qquad
\mu_{i+1}:=\mu_i
+\varepsilon^{-1}\delta_i.
\end{equation*}

Then

\begin{equation}
\delta_{i}<\min(
\varepsilon ^{2i},\mu_i),\qquad
\mu_i<\varepsilon ^{3}\qquad\text{for all
$i=1,2,\dots$}
\end{equation}
